[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186078552 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/id #uuid "3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122322" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9ceef67f02c022065be31de7ec1b6785d270c194aee29c4d0a20707998932134.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{BC}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠B.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) & =\\frac{BC}{12} \\\\ BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12(0.788\\,01…) \\\\  & =9.456\\,12… \\\\  & ≈9.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" "answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" "answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" "answer-093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/id #uuid "26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/id #uuid "36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/id #uuid "51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer/id #uuid "5a69af37-0c06-5df1-aa78-ca7c1546903d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4" :answer/id #uuid "093e66c5-68b2-5de8-be74-d3e1b20f43d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/id #uuid "db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/math-academy-id "q-122353" :question/problem "![](images/77/77242f149dc99e0641e6e095d02aeeb1fffdf764ee664cfcc02e659f9d0e03b0.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}$ rounded to one decimal place." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the adjacent leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AC}$ hypotenuse to the given angle $∠A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{AC} \\\\ AC\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{(0.927\\,18…)} \\\\  & =7.549\\,74… \\\\  & ≈7.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/id #uuid "dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" "answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" "answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" "answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/id #uuid "a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/id #uuid "a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/id #uuid "b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/id #uuid "f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/id #uuid "720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078725 :question/problem "A triangle $△LMN$ has $m∠L={90}^{∘},$ $m∠N={37}^{∘},$ and $LM=8.$ Find the length of $\\overset{―}{LN}$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the given triangle.\n\n![](images/38/38dcba98867c158c671b35ec033fa1ec55c8cedc67466ebe981de9fbbae314e9.png)\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LM}$ opposite to the given angle $∠N$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LN}$ adjacent$∠N.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =\\frac{8}{LN} \\\\ LN\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =8 \\\\ LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{(0.753\\,55…)} \\\\  & =10.616\\,35… \\\\  & ≈11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075226 :answer-field/correct 17592186075231 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453" :activity/id #uuid "576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453" :activity/title "Calculating Side Lengths of Right Triangles Using Trigonometry" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048410 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017"] :activity/first-step "step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :step/id #uuid "632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :step/content "question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :step/next "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :step/id #uuid "1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :step/content "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :step/next "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :step/id #uuid "8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :step/content 17592186078725 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/id #uuid "3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b"] ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122322"] ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9ceef67f02c022065be31de7ec1b6785d270c194aee29c4d0a20707998932134.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{BC}$ rounded to one decimal place."] ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to the given angle $∠B.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) & =\\frac{BC}{12} \\\\ BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12\\operatorname{cos}⁡({38}^{∘}) \\\\  & =12(0.788\\,01…) \\\\  & =9.456\\,12… \\\\  & ≈9.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."] ["question-3c476ad6-03e3-57c6-ac0c-7d3e461a358b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b7b0522-84f1-5956-962e-86aea240df5c"] ["answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/id #uuid "26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae"] ["answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-26256598-94e5-56e9-a905-4f642b7536ae" :answer/value "7.8"] ["answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/id #uuid "36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038"] ["answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-36140525-504a-5b6d-8a94-c1d35b940038" :answer/value "8.5"] ["answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/id #uuid "51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70"] ["answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5e14-8481-2347a142bf70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-51d7af68-0a6e-5