cfcc02e659f9d0e03b0.png)\n\nGiven the triangle above, find the length of $\\overset{―}{AC}$ rounded to one decimal place."] ["question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, note that we are given the length of the adjacent leg $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{AC}$ hypotenuse to the given angle $∠A.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the adjacent leg to the hypotenuse is *cosine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{AC} \\\\ AC\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({22}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{(0.927\\,18…)} \\\\  & =7.549\\,74… \\\\  & ≈7.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."] ["question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/id #uuid "dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694"] ["answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/id #uuid "a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580"] ["answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580" :answer/value "7.4"] ["answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/id #uuid "a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53"] ["answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53" :answer/value "7.5"] ["answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/id #uuid "b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21"] ["answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21" :answer/value "8.2"] ["answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/id #uuid "f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6"] ["answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6" :answer/value "8.5"] ["answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/id #uuid "720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301"] ["answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301" :answer/value "9.5"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/correct "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/choices "answer-a4475272-1254-5374-b9a5-1ae13bf40580"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/choices "answer-a27513fc-52d7-5aae-8114-61b988f68c53"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/choices "answer-b7f65878-4423-5003-bb30-a8b179c3fc21"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/choices "answer-f715c199-77ad-5e4d-b6a4-19176a3b13e6"] ["answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694" :answer-field/choices "answer-720d9d1c-5ab9-50e9-b083-1d77e7c43301"] ["question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-dee662f8-4fb6-5dbb-876b-c57ec504e694"] [17592186078552 :knowledge-point/questions "question-db59e458-8e99-5a95-814f-8adc8a6a9836"] [17592186078725 :question/problem "A triangle $△LMN$ has $m∠L={90}^{∘},$ $m∠N={37}^{∘},$ and $LM=8.$ Find the length of $\\overset{―}{LN}$ rounded to the nearest integer."] [17592186078725 :question/worked-solution "For an angle $\\theta $ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{adjacent leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the given triangle.\n\n![](images/38/38dcba98867c158c671b35ec033fa1ec55c8cedc67466ebe981de9fbbae314e9.png)\n\nNotice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LM}$ opposite to the given angle $∠N$ and wish to find the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{LN}$ adjacent$∠N.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the adjacent leg is *tangent*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{adjacent leg}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =\\frac{8}{LN} \\\\ LN\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘}) & =8 \\\\ LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({37}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{(0.753\\,55…)} \\\\  & =10.616\\,35… \\\\  & ≈11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."] [17592186078725 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186075226 :answer-field/correct 17592186075231] ["activity-576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453" :activity/id #uuid "576dc7b4-9f19-5b00-813c-ad7409e11453"] ["step-632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d" :step/id #uuid "632f2b5c-59a9-5ba2-801e-afe343c8884d"] ["step-1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92" :step/id #uuid "1a29101a-51c6-5a17-9630-96d384c00f92"] ["step-8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017" :step/id #uuid "8229b54b-7fdd-521b-bccb-cd2fbf390017"] 